[tab title="Read & Write Paths"]

## Critical Paths

[columns]
[col]
[section title="Write Path — Create Short URL" style=card]
[timeline color=blue]
- Step 1: Client → POST /shorten — API Gateway validates JWT + rate limit
- Step 2: URL Service — normalise URL, strip tracking params
- Step 3: Dedup check — query Redis/DB: same user + long_url exists?
- Step 4: ID Generation — Snowflake node generates 64-bit ID → Base62 encode → 7-char code
- Step 5: Collision check — GET Cassandra by short_code; retry with +1 sequence if collision
- Step 6: Dual write — write to Cassandra (CL=QUORUM), write-through to Redis
- Step 7: Event publish — Kafka topic url-created (async, non-blocking)
- Step 8: Response — return {short_url, expires_at, analytics_url} in < 50ms
[/timeline]
[/section]
[/col]
[col]
[section title="Read Path — Redirect" style=card]
[timeline color=green]
- Step 1: Client → GET /abc1234 — CDN checks edge cache (85% hit rate)
- Step 2: CDN miss → API Gateway → Redirect Service pod
- Step 3: L1 cache — in-process LRU lookup (< 0.1ms, ~60% hit)
- Step 4: L2 cache — Redis Cluster lookup (< 1ms, ~35% hit of remainder)
- Step 5: DB read — Cassandra LOCAL_QUORUM, nearest replica (< 5ms)
- Step 6: Cache warm — async write-back to Redis + CDN surrogate-key tag
- Step 7: Expiry check — is expires_at in past? → 410 Gone
- Step 8: Click event — fire-and-forget publish to Kafka (async goroutine)
- Step 9: 302 redirect — Location: {long_url}, total p99 < 10ms
[/timeline]
[/section]
[/col]
[/columns]

[code lang=go title="redirect_handler.go"
func (h *Handler) Redirect(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    code := chi.URLParam(r, "code")

    // L1: in-process LRU (~0.1ms)
    if url, ok := h.l1.Get(code); ok {
        h.publishClick(code, r) // fire-and-forget
        http.Redirect(w, r, url, http.StatusFound)
        return
    }

    // L2: Redis cluster (~1ms)
    url, err := h.redis.Get(r.Context(), "url:"+code).Result()
    if err == nil {
        h.l1.Set(code, url)
        h.publishClick(code, r)
        http.Redirect(w, r, url, http.StatusFound)
        return
    }

    // L3: Cassandra (LOCAL_QUORUM)
    row, err := h.db.GetURL(r.Context(), code)
    if err != nil || !row.IsActive {
        http.NotFound(w, r)
        return
    }
    if row.ExpiresAt != nil && row.ExpiresAt.Before(time.Now()) {
        http.Error(w, "Gone", http.StatusGone)
        return
    }

    // warm both caches async
    go h.redis.Set(context.Background(), "url:"+code, row.LongURL, 24*time.Hour)
    h.l1.Set(code, row.LongURL)

    h.publishClick(code, r)
    http.Redirect(w, r, row.LongURL, http.StatusFound)
}
]

[chart type=pie title="Redirect Request Served By"
  CDN_Edge=85 Redis_L1=9 Redis_L2=5 Cassandra=1
]

[callout icon=💡 title="302 vs 301 Trade-off" text="Use 302 (Found) instead of 301 (Moved Permanently). 301 is cached by browsers indefinitely — you lose analytics and can't update the target. 302 always hits your servers, enabling click tracking and link editing. CDN handles caching at scale." color=blue]

[/tab]
[tab title="Data Model"]

## Data Model Design

[section title="URLs Table (Cassandra)" style=card]
[table cols="Column,Type,Notes"
  short_code | text (PK) | Base62, 7 chars, partition key
  long_url | text | Original URL, max 2048 chars
  user_id | uuid | Owner; null for anonymous
  created_at | timestamp | Snowflake-derived
  expires_at | timestamp | Null = never
  is_custom | boolean | Custom alias flag
  click_count | counter | Approximate; Cassandra counter column
  is_active | boolean | Soft delete / deactivate
]

[code lang=sql title="urls.cql"
CREATE TABLE urls (
    short_code  text        PRIMARY KEY,
    long_url    text        NOT NULL,
    user_id     uuid,
    created_at  timestamp   NOT NULL,
    expires_at  timestamp,
    is_custom   boolean     DEFAULT false,
    is_active   boolean     DEFAULT true
) WITH default_time_to_live = 0
  AND compaction = {'class': 'LeveledCompactionStrategy'}
  AND gc_grace_seconds = 86400;

-- counter table (separate in Cassandra)
CREATE TABLE url_clicks (
    short_code  text    PRIMARY KEY,
    click_count counter
);
]
[/section]

[section title="Users Table (PostgreSQL)" style=card]
[table cols="Column,Type,Notes"
  user_id | uuid (PK) | —
  email | text UNIQUE | —
  plan_tier | enum | free / pro / enterprise
  rate_limit | int | Max creates/day
  created_at | timestamp | —
]

[code lang=sql title="users.sql"
CREATE TYPE plan_tier AS ENUM ('free', 'pro', 'enterprise');

CREATE TABLE users (
    user_id    uuid        PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    email      text        UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    plan_tier  plan_tier   NOT NULL DEFAULT 'free',
    rate_limit int         NOT NULL DEFAULT 50,
    created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_users_email ON users(email);
]

[callout icon=💡 title="Why two databases?" text="URLs table is read-heavy, append-only, and benefits from Cassandra's partition-key lookup. Users table is relational with joins and ACID needs — PostgreSQL is the right tool." color=blue]
[/section]

[section title="Click Events (ClickHouse)" style=card]
[table cols="Column,Type,Notes"
  short_code | LowCardinality(String) | Join key
  clicked_at | DateTime64 | Millisecond precision
  country | LowCardinality(String) | MaxMind GeoIP
  city | String | —
  device_type | LowCardinality(String) | mobile / desktop / bot
  referrer_domain | String | Stripped to domain only
  ip_hash | UInt64 | SHA-256 truncated, no PII
]

[code lang=sql title="click_events.sql (ClickHouse)"
CREATE TABLE click_events (
    short_code      LowCardinality(String),
    clicked_at      DateTime64(3),
    country         LowCardinality(String),
    city            String,
    device_type     LowCardinality(String),
    referrer_domain String,
    ip_hash         UInt64
) ENGINE = MergeTree()
PARTITION BY toYYYYMM(clicked_at)
ORDER BY (short_code, clicked_at)
TTL clicked_at + INTERVAL 2 YEAR;
]

[callout icon=⚠️ title="Privacy" text="Raw IP is never stored. ip_hash uses a rotating daily salt — re-identification across days is impossible. GDPR-compliant by design." color=yellow]
[/section]

[section title="Cache Key Design" style=card]
[table cols="Key Pattern,Value,TTL"
  url:{short_code} | long_url string | 24h (sliding)
  user:{user_id}:links | paginated link list JSON | 5 min
  analytics:{short_code}:24h | aggregated click stats | 1h
  ratelimit:{ip}:{minute} | request count | 60s
]
[/section]

[/tab]
[tab title="Scalability & Reliability"]

## Scalability Strategy

[columns]
[col]
[section title="Horizontal Scaling" style=card]
[list style=check]
- Redirect Service: stateless, auto-scale 50→500 pods on CPU/QPS
- URL Write Service: stateless, scale independently
- Cassandra: add nodes, rebalances automatically (virtual nodes)
- Redis: cluster sharding by short_code hash slot
- Kafka: add partitions + consumer group members
[/list]
[/section]
[/col]
[col]
[section title="Multi-Region Active-Active" style=card]
[list style=check]
- 3 regions: US-East, EU-West, AP-Southeast
- Cassandra cross-region replication (async, RF=3 per region)
- Redirect service reads LOCAL_QUORUM — no cross-region latency
- Writes: route to nearest region, async replicate
- Global Load Balancer (Anycast) routes by latency
[/list]
[/section]
[/col]
[/columns]

## Reliability Design
[columns]
[col]
[section title="Failure Modes & Mitigations" style=card]
[table cols="Failure,Detection,Mitigation"
  Redis down | Health check | Fallback to Cassandra; degrade gracefully
  Cassandra node down | Gossip protocol | RF=3; reads still succeed with 2 nodes
  Kafka lag spike | Consumer lag metric | Scale consumers; shed non-critical events
  ID generator down | Heartbeat | Multiple Snowflake nodes; no SPOF
  CDN outage | Synthetic monitor | Origin handles full load; auto-scaled
]
[/section]
[/col]
[col]
[section title="SLO Targets" style=card]
[kpi label="Redirect Availability" value="99.99%" target="99.99%" trend=+0% color=green]
[kpi label="P99 Redirect Latency" value="8ms" target="10ms" trend=-20% color=green]
[kpi label="Write Availability" value="99.95%" target="99.9%" trend=+0.05% color=green]
[kpi label="Analytics Freshness" value="30s" target="60s" trend=-50% color=green]
[/section]
[/col]
[/columns]

